---
title: SignOff capabilities and relations (v4.1.3)
---
flowchart LR
  subgraph L1["① Entry · who calls it"]
    direction TB
    A1["CLI<br/>run · p1..p5 · init · status · doctor<br/>audit · explain · release · mcp · uninstall<br/>--json · --strict · --dry-run · --chain"]
    A2["Git hooks<br/>pre-commit runs the gates<br/>commit-msg checks the trailer<br/>pre-push checks the audit window<br/>existing hooks chained as .local"]
    A3["CI · signoff.yml<br/>same gates, second run<br/>fetch-depth 0 required for audit"]
    A4["Agents<br/>5 MCP tools · one skill<br/>isError mirrors the exit code"]
    A1 ~~~ A2 ~~~ A3 ~~~ A4
  end

  subgraph L2["② Dispatcher · guard.js decides what runs and what counts as pass"]
    direction TB
    D1["Parse<br/>cwd normalised to repo root<br/>SIGNOFF_* env · piped runs filtered"]
    D2["Lock<br/>.signoff/lock/ dir + owner.json<br/>atomic mkdir; dead pid or >10 min reclaimed<br/>wait cap SIGNOFF_LOCK_WAIT_MS=8s"]
    D3["Select gates<br/>five by default<br/>name p1..p5; a hook runs only its stage"]
    D4["Verdict<br/>0 all pass · 1 any gate red · 2 usage or env<br/>no partial pass; --json emits the result"]
    D1 ~~~ D2 ~~~ D3 ~~~ D4
  end

  subgraph L3["③ Five gates · each answers: read → decide → fix"]
    direction TB
    P1["P1 Tests<br/>read: config.test_cmd, else auto-detect<br/>decide: test exit code ≠ 0<br/>fix: pin the command in config"]
    P2["P2 Coverage<br/>read: scenario files, assertion count<br/>decide: below threshold, or no assertions<br/>fix: add assertions; --strict is stricter"]
    P3["P3 Queue<br/>read: status in tasks/id/card.json<br/>decide: not done, or fields missing<br/>fix: finish the card's acceptance criteria"]
    P4["P4 Ledger<br/>read: audit.log hash chain + rollback commit<br/>decide: chain broken, rollback gone, trailer missing<br/>fix: p4 ask/confirm, or roll back"]
    P5["P5 Anti-slop<br/>read: docs added by this change<br/>decide: placeholders · claims without evidence<br/>fix: add evidence or delete it"]
    P1 ~~~ P2 ~~~ P3 ~~~ P4 ~~~ P5
  end

  subgraph L4["④ State machine · what happens inside one commit"]
    direction TB
    S1["pre-commit<br/>all five pass → marker {tree, mode} written"]
    S2["commit-msg<br/>marker.tree == HEAD tree ?<br/>yes → append the Signoff-Pass trailer"]
    S3["pre-push<br/>every commit in the audit window checked<br/>missing trailer = red"]
    S4["CI<br/>gates + audit again<br/>no git identity means no fake pass"]
    S1 ~~~ S2 ~~~ S3 ~~~ S4
  end

  subgraph L5["⑤ Artifacts · judgment leaves evidence"]
    direction TB
    F1["passed<br/>tree + mode(pass|skip) + ts<br/>invalidated when tree changes"]
    F2["audit.log<br/>append-only hash chain: prevHash · action · rollback"]
    F3["installed.json<br/>install-point sha / time / version<br/>left edge of the audit window"]
    F4["commit message<br/>Signoff-Pass: tree<br/>--no-verify is the only hole"]
    F5["config.json<br/>thresholds · test command · P5 word list"]
    F1 ~~~ F2 ~~~ F3 ~~~ F4 ~~~ F5
  end

  subgraph L6["⑥ External dependencies · only two are hard requirements"]
    direction TB
    X1["Node ≥ 18<br/>pure JS · no build step · no native modules"]
    X2["git<br/>hook location · history · ancestor checks"]
    X3["Test runner<br/>whatever the repo uses; falls back when absent"]
    X4["Python · peer tests only<br/>never invoked at runtime"]
    X5["GitHub Actions<br/>optional, --no-ci skips it"]
    X1 ~~~ X2 ~~~ X3 ~~~ X4 ~~~ X5
  end

  L1 -->|calls| L2
  L2 -->|picks gates per stage| L3
  L3 -->|writes marker / trailer| L4
  L4 -->|persists| L5
  L5 -->|audit comparison| L6


